  "id": "nmda-receptor",
  "term": "NMDA receptor",
  "definition": "An NMDA receptor is a type of glutamate receptor that forms an ion channel activated by N-methyl-D-aspartate. It opens efficiently only when glycine is also bound, is regulated by voltage-dependent magnesium binding, and is notable for letting calcium pass in ways important for neuronal plasticity and excitotoxicity.",
